From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:10:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: iomfb_m4: accept the J604 allocate_buffer
 alignment

On J604 (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M4, DCP firmware 26.6.2) the first D451
allocate_buffer request after IOMFB start is rejected, which quarantines
the retained session and fails the DCP bind with -EINVAL. The request
(logged by the previous commit) is:

  03 07 00 00  00 10 00 00 00 00 00 00  00 10 00 00  00 00 00 5b

type 0x703, size 0x1000, alignment 0x1000, bytes 16-18 zero. Only the
alignment check fails: it accepts exactly 4, the value the qualified
firmware sends.

Every object this callback hands out is 16 KiB aligned in both the
SID23 and the SID16 address space (the allocator output is checked for
that before it is published), so any power-of-two alignment up to
16 KiB is already met. Accept those instead of the single value. The
iomfb_v26_6 path makes the same check (power of two, at most SZ_16K).

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-memory.h | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-memory.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-memory.h
index 0716c432f1..4076cc6131 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-memory.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-memory.h
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #define APPLE_DCP_M4_MEMORY_H
 
 #include <linux/errno.h>
+#include <linux/log2.h>
 #include <linux/string.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/unaligned.h>
@@ -49,9 +50,15 @@ static inline int dcp_m4_memory_callback(struct dcp_m4_memory *memory,
 	if (method == 451) {
 		size = get_unaligned_le64(in + 4);
 		align = get_unaligned_le32(in + 12);
-		/* The qualified internal firmware requests alignment exponent 4. */
+		/*
+		 * The qualified internal firmware sends 4 here, the J604 26.6.2
+		 * firmware 0x1000. Every object is 16 KiB aligned in both address
+		 * spaces (checked below), which meets both and any power-of-two byte
+		 * alignment up to 16 KiB.
+		 */
 		if (get_unaligned_le32(in) != 0x703 || !size || size > DCP_M4_MEMORY_MAX ||
-		    align != 4 || in[16] || in[17] || in[18])
+		    !is_power_of_2(align) || align > DCP_M4_MEMORY_PAGE ||
+		    in[16] || in[17] || in[18])
 			goto failed;
 		/* Byte 19 is padding, observed nonzero in otherwise valid requests. */
 		size = (size + DCP_M4_MEMORY_PAGE - 1) & ~(u64)(DCP_M4_MEMORY_PAGE - 1);
